
@{
    ViewBag.Title = "Privacy Policy";
}

<style>
    .privacy-hero {
        background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f172a, #1e3a8a);
        color: white;
        padding: 65px 20px;
        text-align: center;
    }

    .privacy-content {
        max-width: 900px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 60px 20px;
    }

    .privacy-content h2 {
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #0f172a;
        margin-top: 40px;
        margin-bottom: 15px;
    }

    .privacy-content p,
    .privacy-content li {
        color: #64748b;
        line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .privacy-content ul {
        padding-left: 25px;
    }

    .last-updated {
        color: #94a3b8;
        font-size: 14px;
        margin-top: 15px;
    }
</style>


<!-- Hero -->
<section class="privacy-hero">
    <div class="container">
        <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>

        <p class="lead mb-0 mt-3">
            Your privacy and data security matter to us.
        </p>

        <div class="last-updated">
            Last Updated: @DateTime.Now.ToString("MMMM dd, yyyy")
        </div>
    </div>
</section>


<!-- Content -->
<section>
    <div class="privacy-content">

        <p>
            Welcome to <strong>CoursePortal</strong>. This Privacy Policy
            explains how CoursePortal collects, uses, stores, and protects
            information when you use our website and services.
        </p>


        <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

        <p>
            When you create an account or use CoursePortal, we may collect
            information such as:
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>Name</li>
            <li>Email address</li>
            <li>Account login information</li>
            <li>Student and course enrollment information</li>
            <li>Information you voluntarily provide through your profile</li>
        </ul>


        <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>

        <p>
            The information we collect is used to provide and improve
            CoursePortal services. This may include:
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>Creating and managing user accounts</li>
            <li>Managing student profiles</li>
            <li>Managing course enrollments</li>
            <li>Providing access to courses and related features</li>
            <li>Maintaining and improving system security</li>
            <li>Improving the overall user experience</li>
        </ul>


        <h2>3. Account Security</h2>

        <p>
            We take reasonable measures to protect user information from
            unauthorized access, modification, disclosure, or destruction.
            Users are responsible for keeping their account credentials
            confidential.
        </p>


        <h2>4. Data Sharing</h2>

        <p>
            CoursePortal does not sell or rent personal information to third
            parties. Information may only be accessed by authorized users
            or administrators when necessary for providing the services
            offered by the platform.
        </p>


        <h2>5. Cookies</h2>

        <p>
            CoursePortal may use cookies or similar technologies to maintain
            login sessions, remember user preferences, and improve the
            functionality of the website.
        </p>


        <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>

        <p>
            We retain account and academic information for as long as
            necessary to provide the services or fulfill legitimate
            administrative requirements.
        </p>


        <h2>7. User Rights</h2>

        <p>
            Depending on the circumstances, users may request access to,
            correction of, or deletion of their personal information.
            Requests can be made through the appropriate administrator.
        </p>


        <h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>

        <p>
            CoursePortal is intended for educational use. Users should
            provide accurate information and should not use the platform
            in violation of applicable age or privacy requirements.
        </p>


        <h2>9. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

        <p>
            This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time to reflect
            changes to the CoursePortal system or its practices. Any changes
            will be reflected on this page.
        </p>


        <h2>10. Contact Us</h2>

        <p>
            If you have questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy,
            please contact the CoursePortal administrator through the
            contact information provided on the website.
        </p>

    </div>
</section>
